stream
From: Dana Whitfield <dana.whitfield@hangs-gc.example>
To: Tax preparation <tax@finance-demo.example>
Subject: HANGS General Contracting Q3 2026 Seattle business tax return
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 10:15:00 -0800
Message-ID: <HGC-26Q3-SEA@hangs-gc.example>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="=_HGC_26Q3_seattle_return"

--=_HGC_26Q3_seattle_return
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hello,

Attached are the Q3 2026 billing register by city and the Q3 general ledger f=
or HANGS General Contracting LP. The Seattle account details, the job list, t=
he Q1 and Q2 Seattle returns, the state returns for July to September and the=
 invoice for change order 6 on Pier 9 Lofts are in the shared folder.

We missed the October 31 due date for the Q3 Seattle return while I was out. =
Please prepare it now as a draft for review; we will file and pay it ourselve=
s in FileLocal. It is separate from the state returns we file in My DOR.

Duwamish Gateway sits across the Seattle and Tukwila line. Our project manage=
r thinks about 60% of the work was on the Seattle parcel, but we do not have =
a survey split or a cost split yet, so everything was coded to Seattle.

We wrote off the Fremont Bakehouse balance (invoice HGC-25-0917) on September=
 30. That invoice was reported as Seattle revenue on our Q4 2025 Seattle retu=
rn.

Dana Whitfield
Controller, HANGS General Contracting

--=_HGC_26Q3_seattle_return
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet
Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64
Content-Disposition: attachment;
 filename="Q3 2026 billing register by city.xlsx"
MIME-Version: 1.0

